  "split_decision": "Extract only the existing-provider wrapper of an actual supplied universal conclusion. Mixed own-provider interfaces keep their complete actual data and independent named proposition proofs in exact archives, without narrowed fields or a new legacy self-import.",
  "review_notes": [
    "The complete record genuinely stores an AdelicCriticalLineContract and an actual AllZerosOnCriticalLine conclusion under every original C/F/nabla/H/e/K dependency. Its independent fixedTensorSuppliesAlignment : Prop and supplied proof do not define a function or relation from a fixed tensor to that conclusion.",
    "The genuine theorem directly projects B.alignmentConclusion, without using K.existsFixedTensor, any individual tensor, or the independent named proposition/proof. Do not infer an independent fixed-tensor-to-critical-line derivation from its name.",
    "AllZerosOnCriticalLine is an actual universal pivot equality over the contract's supplied Zeros type and chosen zeroData. Zeros may be empty; no assertion relates these supplied data completely to actual analytic L-function zeros. The already supplied criticalLineBridge is also a typed assumption, not derived spectral or analytic forcing.",
    "Preserve both complete mixed own-provider commands and all documentation/imports in exact archives. Extracting a subset would narrow the record, and extracting the local consequence would require a new legacy self-provider import absent from this source. Neither is introduced."
  ],
